# {{.Name}}

A grist application, scaffolded by `grist new {{.Name}}`: items added to
a store that holds at most five of each (`add-item`, refused `invalid` or
`full`), shown (`show-item`), tallied after each addition (the
`tally` processor) and sent to a warehouse (the `shelve` processor,
calling `Receive` of the declared dependency `Warehouse`: in a
simulation, its default double, lossy). It is checked against its Quint model with nothing
annotated: grist records every block's step, and the model's skeleton
and both bindings are generated from the App's catalog.

| file | what it is |
|---|---|
| [app.go](app.go), [commands.go](commands.go), [queries.go](queries.go), [processors.go](processors.go), [deps.go](deps.go) | the events, the read model (`stock`, keyed by item), the command, the query, the processors, the warehouse (a dependency and its call) |
| [model/{{.Name}}.qnt](model/{{.Name}}.qnt) | written by hand: the rules the skeleton calls (each command's outcome, events and the reads it needs, the query's answer, the processors' events, the warehouse's request) and the invariants, each marked for its binding (`// grist: invariant`) |
| [model/{{.Name}}_gen.qnt](model/{{.Name}}_gen.qnt), `*.binding.yaml`, [model/grist.qnt](model/grist.qnt) | generated: `go run ./cmd/{{.Name}} model` (never edit them; `TestGenerated` fails when they are stale) |
| [cmd/{{.Name}}](cmd/{{.Name}}/main.go) | the binary (`grist.Main`): `model`, `catalog`, `verify`, `serve -db sqlite:PATH` |
| [testdata/mutants](testdata/mutants) | `noCapacity`: the capacity check left out |

## Which check catches which mutant

| test | configuration | catches |
|---|---|---|
| `TestFaithful` | one tenant, three clients, commit faults, node crashes, a lossy API and warehouse | nothing: `Conforms`, `All(Settles)`, commit faults reached, every block of the catalog taken (`gristtest.Exercised`) |
| `TestFaithfulAtClients` | the same runs at the clients, linearized | nothing: `Conforms` |
| `TestFull` | two clients filling one item, no faults | nothing: `None(Rejects("addItem"))` (the mutant's contrast) |
| `TestMutant` (`noCapacity`) | the same | `Some(Rejects("addItem"))`: an addition past the capacity commits where the model refuses it |
| `TestRealHTTP` | the real tier: SQLite, real HTTP, the warehouse's default double in process, every fifth answer lost (gristtest.Tier) | nothing: both bindings conform, every answer has its store-side step |
| `TestGenerated` | the generated files against the catalog | a block changed without regenerating |

## Next

Add a block (an event, a command, a processor, a dependency's call) in Go, regenerate (`go
run ./cmd/{{.Name}} model`: it names each new hole and a stub for it),
fill the holes in `model/{{.Name}}.qnt`, mark the invariants, and write a
mutant per claim. skills/grist says how.

```sh
go test -short ./...           # every claim (needs quint on PATH)
./run-demo.sh
MUTATION=no-capacity ./run-demo.sh
```
